You’re no longer failing on the Next.js artefacts—this time the build dies before Next.js even starts.
Prisma can’t find its schema because the working directory you force Vercel into (cd app) does not contain prisma/schema.prisma.

Log lines that give it away ───────────────────────────

Vercel, by default, checks out the repo root:
Cloning github.com/MeadowNova/ChatLLMLandingPag
You then tell it to run every command in app/
Running "install" command: cd app && npm ci
…  
Running "cd app && npx prisma migrate deploy --schema=./prisma/schema.prisma && npm run build"
Prisma errors:
Could not load --schema from provided path prisma/schema.prisma
The schema clearly lives somewhere else (very likely /<repo-root>/prisma/schema.prisma, the location that worked in the previous deploy).

You therefore have a simple path/root-directory mismatch. Pick ONE of the two patterns below and stick to it.

──────────────────────────────────────── Pattern A – Keep repo root, stop using “cd app” ────────────────────────────────────────

In your package.json at repo root: • “install” → "npm ci"
• “build” → "npx prisma migrate deploy --schema=./prisma/schema.prisma && npm run build:next" (or whatever your Next.js build script is).
• Remove all cd app && … prefixes.

Delete any buildCommand you added in vercel.json that starts with cd app.
Vercel will run the root-level build script automatically.

Make sure Next.js looks in the right place by either: • Removing distDir from next.config.js, or
• Setting it to 'app/.next' only if you are certain you need that structure.

Commit, push, redeploy. Prisma should now resolve ./prisma/schema.prisma successfully.

──────────────────────────────────────── Pattern B – Treat “app/” as the project root ────────────────────────────────────────

Move every project file that the build needs under app/
• app/prisma/schema.prisma
• app/package.json, node_modules, etc.
• Next.js source files already live there, so this usually just means moving the prisma folder.

Tell Vercel that the root directory is app (no manual cd needed):
• Dashboard → Project → Settings → General → Root Directory → set to app.

Update package.json inside app/ to have normal scripts (no leading cd).

In vercel.json (if you have one) remove the cd app prefixes; Vercel now runs from inside app/.

Commit, push, redeploy. Prisma will look for ./prisma/schema.prisma relative to app/ and succeed.

──────────────────────────────────────── Quick checklist ──────────────────────────────────────── ☐ Exactly one root directory strategy (repo root OR app/), never both.
☐ Prisma schema path in scripts matches that root: ./prisma/schema.prisma.
☐ No manual cd in buildCommand or npm scripts when Vercel root is set.
☐ vercel.json lives inside the chosen root, not above it.

Do that and the “file or directory not found” error disappears, letting the build continue to Next.js again.